  "id": "intraday-ranges",
  "title": "Intraday Swings",
  "turns": [
    {
      "jobId": "4bfdbd81-6893-40d7-91d9-ff4a3b668948",
      "question": "Among the 50 most liquid US stocks, which sessions from March 2 through March 12, 2026 had the widest intraday price ranges? For each, how did it trade from open to close, and how much of its volume came in the last 30 minutes?",
      "submittedAt": "2026-10-01T18:35:24.760073Z",
      "completedAt": "2026-10-01T18:35:41.236743Z",
      "status": "success",
      "report": {
        "markdown": "Among the 50 most liquid US stocks, the sessions with the widest intraday price ranges from **March 2–12, 2026** were dominated by **CRCL** (Circle Internet Group) and **APP** (AppLovin). The table below shows the top 10 sessions ranked by intraday range, with each session’s open-to-close move and the share of volume that occurred in the last 30 minutes (including the closing auction).\n\n| Rank | Asset | Session | Intraday Range | Open → Close Return | Last 30-min Volume Share |\n|------|-------|---------|----------------|----------------------|---------------------------|\n| 1 | CRCL | 2026-03-02 | 20.42% | +19.06% | 16.18% |\n| 2 | CRCL | 2026-03-03 | 14.45% | +8.78% | 12.57% |\n| 3 | BMNR | 2026-03-02 | 12.43% | +7.78% | 17.37% |\n| 4 | CRCL | 2026-03-11 | 10.45% | –5.81% | 16.82% |\n| 5 | INTC | 2026-03-09 | 9.89% | +6.55% | 26.12% |\n| 6 | APP | 2026-03-04 | 9.44% | +8.76% | 19.04% |\n| 7 | APP | 2026-03-03 | 9.37% | +6.64% | 13.73% |\n| 8 | APP | 2026-03-10 | 9.30% | –7.14% | 17.14% |\n| 9 | MU | 2026-03-09 | 9.04% | +6.89% | 18.82% |\n| 10 | COIN | 2026-03-04 | 8.53% | +6.59% | 15.95% |\n\n[1]\n\n**Key observations**\n- CRCL’s March 2 session had the widest range (20.4%), driven by a massive open-to-close rally of 19.1% on heavy volume (25.3M shares). Only 16.2% of that volume came in the final 30 minutes.\n- CRCL appears three times in the top 10 (Mar 2, Mar 3, Mar 11), with the Mar 11 session being the only down-day (–5.8% close-to-close) but still a wide range.\n- APP also appears three times (Mar 3, 4, 10), with the Mar 10 session showing a 7.1% decline on a 9.3% range.\n- Volume in the last 30 minutes varied widely: INTC on Mar 9 saw 26.1% of its volume late, while APP on Mar 3 saw just 13.7%.\n\n**Limitations**: Metrics cover the regular trading session only; the last 30 minutes include the closing auction. The scan covered 450 sessions across the 50 most liquid stocks.\n\n## Sources\n\n- [1] Market analytics result — intraday scan — evidence `hermes-receipt:c132207bd7f16138bf473c4c55e0962953315a58efff4d25f19a37f709ad727b`",
